nodecode-neuralwatt is a rewrite of 0xGingi's 0xGingi/neuralwatt-hermes:

  https://github.com/0xGingi/neuralwatt-hermes
  commit 008e6147b9376527579b4446467db40d9423f8da

MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 0xGingi (LICENSE)

The nine read-only tools are rewritten in Common Lisp against Nodecode's cell
contract, with the same endpoints, the same parameters and the same data: service
health, the model catalog and its prices, quota, a combined dashboard, energy,
usage breakdowns, request rows and session analytics. What changed is the
plumbing around them: the key is read from the cell's own config section rather
than from the harness's secret scope, every answer is formatted text rather than
a JSON string, and the aggregation a comparison or a ranking needs is computed
here from the same per-request pages. Two shapes of the original are left out
because the contract has no equivalent: its per-tool emoji and toolset label,
and its `check_fn`, which hid the six account tools when no key was set -- this
cell needs the key to start at all, so all nine tools appear together. The
keyless call of the three public views (health, models, prices) is therefore not
kept, and neither is the `NEURALWATT_BASE_URL` environment override: the base URL
is a section member, which is where a Nodecode cell declares its host.
